NP-HALL-CHEM-AIR HA-O-ION-01 (VARIANT member of the unweighted BEB / Thompson pair, OQ-HA-02). e + O(3P) -> O(+) + 2e. Byte-identical copy of docs/chemistry/o_o2/v0/tables/ionization_O_thompson1995.dat (sha256 a1fe0dcdf786ee84a5de58ac996bac8130318298103575b383450fcd1e40e6b4; v0 DRAFT, immutable), built by docs/chemistry/o_o2/v0/build_tables_nist107_o.py with abep_sim/rate_tables.py. Cross section: Thompson, Shah & Gilbody, J. Phys. B 28, 1321 (1995), measured points as tabulated by NIST SRD 107 (https://physics.nist.gov/cgi-bin/Ionization/merge.php?file=OI--&mode=ASCII, raw sha256 76df7f7a223a803ab5902eeae0b557ffb2d3317ba692a37676851781a1d225d8, not committed); 47 points 14.1-2000 eV; linear ramp from sigma(13.618 eV) = 0 to the 14.1 eV point (assumed segment); held above 2000 eV. Recommended by SONG2026 Sec. III.D. Whether the NIST column is the O+ partial or the counting total is not stated (verify, VER-HA-03). Header 13.618 eV = O ionization energy (Itikawa & Ichimura, JPCRD 19, 637 (1990) Table 2.1). Energy column = mean electron energy 3/2 Te. Evidence level 4 (docs/EVIDENCE.md); quantity type: measured as tabulated, threshold segment assumed. Rebuild needs the NIST raw file (host blocked here); the copy is checked against the v0 sha256 by abep_chem::hall_air.
